```css
/* H1 gutter: center the collapse caret + bullet on the heading's first line.

   Roam ships `.rm-heading-level-1 > .rm-block-main > .rm-block__controls
   { padding-top: 12px }`. That box is already `display:flex; align-items:center;
   min-height:42px`, so the padding shifts the centering down by exactly half —
   the bullet lands padding-top/2 = 6px BELOW the text center.

   Measured live (Readwisenotes, CDP): offset = padding-top / 2, and
   padding-top:0 gives -0.02px. So zero is the centered value, not a magic number. */

.rm-heading-level-1 > .rm-block-main > .rm-block__controls {
  padding-top: 2 !important;
}

/* Same +padTop/2 offset exists on H2 (8px -> 4px low) and H3 (5px -> 2.5px low).
   Uncomment to center those too:

.rm-heading-level-2 > .rm-block-main > .rm-block__controls,
.rm-heading-level-3 > .rm-block-main > .rm-block__controls {
  padding-top: 0 !important;
}
*/```
